# Coding standards (Global)

- Match existing repo conventions first (lint/format/naming); do not introduce new styles casually.
- If ambiguous: prefer **functional-first** style, small pure functions, explicit data flow.
- Minimize churn: smallest change that solves the problem; no drive-by refactors.
- Preserve public APIs unless explicitly asked; call out breaking changes clearly.
- Error handling: don’t swallow errors; return/throw actionable messages.
- Logging: no noisy logs; never log secrets/PII.
- Types: avoid `any`/weak typing; constrain with enums/unions where helpful.
- Dependencies: prefer built-ins; add new deps only if justified and scoped.
